<p>This is&#8230; you get articles like this from time to time, where the Foundation appears to be missing things that are blindingly obvious to the reader. What sets this apart, however, is that it's exactly the kind of situation where an institution like the Foundation <em>would</em> be idiotic- a situation where the alternative to stupidity is acknowledging that you've done something evil.</p>
<p>Which means that it's also a better-than-average example of 'the Foundation does something evil'; you can see the logic behind the decisions they made, as well as after-the-fact excuses for when it went bad. Rather than it just being openly amoral, the bureaucracy is trying to cover its own ass and justify itself.</p>
<p>+1</p>

